{"status":"success","data":[{"siteid":30965,"sitename":"Palomaa","sitedescription":"Small mire located close to the northern limit of pine forest in eastern Finnish Lapland. To the south, forest areas are dominated almost exclusively by Scots Pine (Pinus sylvestris) while, to the north, the regional vegetation type is mountain birch woodland (Betula pubescens ssp. czerepanovii).","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[27.19048,69.2778]}","altitude":200,"recdatecreated":"2024-04-11T13:38:50.000Z","collectionunits":[{"handle":"PALOMAA","datasets":[{"datasetid":58530,"datasettype":"pollen"}],"collectionunit":"Palomaa core","collectionunitid":42184,"collectionunittype":"Core"}]}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}